    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0424" n="308" xml:id="pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.304M28/71.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 165.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                        enclosed<anchor n="1" xml:id="d434-f1"/> translation of newspaper comment
                    concerning the wreck of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> and the honors to
                    the victims. * * *</p>
                <p>I have not ventured to report the ceremonies themselves in the belief that a full
                    report will be made to the War and Navy Departments by the officers directly
                    concerned.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
